+gstack-learnings-log — append one learning to
+  $GSTACK_HOME/projects/<slug>/learnings.jsonl   (default ~/.gstack)
+
+usage:
+  gstack-learnings-log '<json>'        one record, a single JSON object
+  gstack-learnings-log --file <path>   read the record from a file
+  gstack-learnings-log -               read the record from stdin
+  gstack-learnings-log --schema        print the record's JSON Schema
+  gstack-learnings-log --help          this text
+
+fields (enforced rules marked; unknown fields pass through):
+EOF
+    printf '%s' "$RECORD_SCHEMA" | bun -e '
+const s = JSON.parse(await Bun.stdin.text());
+const req = s.required || [];
+for (const k of Object.keys(s.properties)) {
+  const v = s.properties[k];
